          <declname>Line</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Parses an individual <computeroutput>Line</computeroutput> of input. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Nodes from the previous <ref refid="classllvm_1_1symbolize_1_1_markup_parser_1af65477d093fd230a78c34132fd3a6546" kindref="member">parseLine()</ref> call that haven&apos;t yet been extracted by <ref refid="classllvm_1_1symbolize_1_1_markup_parser_1a1eaa76c1f1e142ff478fe1ac0196cab9" kindref="member">nextNode()</ref> are discarded. The nodes returned by <ref refid="classllvm_1_1symbolize_1_1_markup_parser_1a1eaa76c1f1e142ff478fe1ac0196cab9" kindref="member">nextNode()</ref> may reference the input string, so it must be retained by the caller until the last use.</para>
<para>Note that some elements may span multiple lines. If a line ends with the start of one of these elements, then no nodes will be produced until the either the end or something that cannot be part of an element is encountered. This may only occur after multiple calls to <ref refid="classllvm_1_1symbolize_1_1_markup_parser_1af65477d093fd230a78c34132fd3a6546" kindref="member">parseLine()</ref>, corresponding to the lines of the multi-line element. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
